				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/communism-will-win" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(617958); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=617958&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608196096" alt="Communism will win" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=617958)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/communism-will-win" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(617958); return false;" >Communism will win</a></span> <span class="odate time_1474173995 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">18 Sep 2016 04:46</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2629192">
									

<blockquote>
<p>By now you probably all have a lot of concerns and questions. Where am I? How did I get here? What happens next?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>How do I work this? Where <em>is</em> that large automobile?</p>
<p>Anyways, it's competent, but I didn't feel much about it. Patricia is a step up from the D-Class that get used or mentioned in SCPs, but she's ultimately not a memorable character, so the ending did not impact me. There was a distinct lack of moments where the character feels or thinks or does something that is really indicative of who they are and you can <em>feel</em> that, and without that, it goes flat.</p>
<p>It certainly didn't provoke thought either, since there's really not much here that isn't just an elaboration of commonly understood or theorized site lore. The random lottery is the exception to that, or it would be, except I don't believe a word of it. Taking people who will be missed would inevitably cause problems, because someone would look into those mysterious disappearances.</p>
<p>What I would find far more plausible, while still being consistent with the article, is that the Foundation has a way of implanting false memories, and gives the various low-risk abductees memories of a nice family and a comfortable life so that they'll be motivated to cooperate in hopes of seeing them again. This would be pretty cool to explore, but instead, I had to infer it. Oh well.</p>

							</div>

